d the qualifying round and the final round to win his first individual gold medal. Denmark’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/11371"} "Anne Grethe Jensen"] " was second in both rounds to secure the silver medal, while " [:a {:href "/athletes/12126"} "Otto Hofer"] " of Switzerland also placed third in both rounds for the bronze medal. The margins between 1-2, 2-3, and 3-4 were quite large so there was not a lot of competition for the medals. During his Olympic career, which ran from 1960-88, Klimke won eight medals, with two individual bronzes in 1968 and 1976, and team golds in 1964, 1968, 1976, 1984, and 1988."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Grand Prix"] [:th {} "Grand Prix Special"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "75"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12244"} "Reiner Klimke"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/43"} "Ahlerich"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRG.png"}] "FRG"]] [:td {} "1,504"] [:td {} "1,797 (1)"] [:td {} "1,504 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "49"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11371"} "Anne Grethe Jensen"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1597"} "Marzog"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} "1,442"] [:td {} "1,701 (2)"] [:td {} "1,442 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "163"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12126"} "Otto Hofer"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1467"} "Limandus"]]]